# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in. Server-side only — never
# prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_, or it would be shipped to every browser.
#
# Without a key the tutor still works: it answers from the built-in guide
# (the rule engine plus the platform's own lessons and gate reference), and
# says so on every answer.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Or Gemini, used when there is no Anthropic key. From aistudio.google.com.
# The free tier allows about 5 questions a minute per model; the tutor falls
# back from gemini-2.5-flash to gemini-3.5-flash-lite when one is busy or over
# quota, then to the built-in guide. Enable billing on the Google project for
# a classroom. Whichever model answers, the physics firewall checks every
# sentence before it is shown.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Optional. Default gemini-2.5-flash (measured ~1.5s to first word).
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Where the Arena (live 1v1 matches and the ladder) connects. Unset, it uses a
# server on this machine: `npm run dev:server` from the repo root, on :4000.
# To play against the deployed server instead:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_ARENA_URL=wss://quriosity-1.onrender.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is intended here — the browser opens this socket itself.
# It is read at build time, so restart `npm run dev` after changing it.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ARENA_URL=ws://localhost:4000
